{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RationalCoeffRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.RationalCoeffRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.recurrence_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.recurrence_step","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RationalCoeffRecurrence.lean#L80-L94","doc":"The C-finite recurrence **solves for the leading term**: for `n ≥ d`, the\ncoefficient `c n` is determined by the previous `d` values via the kernel\n`-(q 0)⁻¹ · q (j+1)`. This is the \"kernel produces `c_k` from the seed\" engine —\nit makes rigorous the Step-2 statement that the kernel fixes `c_{n}` from the\nlast `d` coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CFinite","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RationalCoeffRecurrence.lean#L74-L78","doc":"`c` is **C-finite of order `d`** with denominator coefficients `q`\n(`q 0 ≠ 0`): the defining constant-coefficient linear recurrence of the\ncoefficients of a proper rational `P/Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pole_reciprocal_is_char_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pole_reciprocal_is_char_root","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RationalCoeffRecurrence.lean#L42-L72","doc":"**Pole ⇒ reciprocal is a characteristic root.** If `u₀ ≠ 0` is a root of the\ndenominator polynomial `∑_{j≤d} q j · X^j`, then `u₀⁻¹` is a root of the\nreversed (characteristic) polynomial `∑_{j≤d} q j · X^(d-j)`.\n\nThis is the `find R ≡ find minimal Q` grounding for the `c_k` recurrence: the\npole `u_substrate` of `F` is exactly such a `u₀`, so `1/u_substrate` is the\ndominant characteristic root of the ladder recurrence — matching the empirical\ntail ratio `c_{k+1}/c_k → 1/u_substrate ≈ 117.4`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}